Kent Paul Dolan wrote:
>   Cavemen, from familiarity with how rock is
>   supposed to look, are also better at noticing
>   traps and secret doors in rough hewn mines and
>   rough (not worked/dressed) stone mazes.
For the other classes that have supposed familiarity with subterranean
realms, thus usually equates to intrinsic searching at level X.

